{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/125154-mortal-remains-not-quite-as-much-a-change-to-endwoments-as-i-hoped","id":125154,"title":"Mortal Remains - not quite as much a change to endwoments as I hoped","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-04T07:27:28-07:00","id":125154,"title":"Mortal Remains - not quite as much a change to endwoments as I hoped","content":"I had been quite looking forward to Mortal Remains since I heard about it, after all, Hunter is a very flexible line with lots of thematic and fun groups, both among the compacts and the conspiracies.<br /> <br /> For me, there has always been one rather nasty side of the line and that was balance and structure.<br /> Endowments, dread Powers are nice and diverse, but especially when it comes to the Endwoments, the ones for the players, it is just really over the place...<br /> I had rather hoped this might be fixed, but while it seems they updated the Godmachine update specific stuff well, it still boils down to this:<br /> <br /> Some Endowments are &quot;pay X dots per Endowment&quot; (Like Relics, Thaumatechnology and Advanced Armory) and some are &quot;buy the Endowment category and get a power per dot&quot; (Castigations and even more so Benedictions which get both a bonus to use and a new power and can buy more powers if needed, that is at least at character creation).<br /> <br /> I never quite liked the fact that this effectively meant that some hunters payed a lot of experience for just one power while other got several powers at the same time.<br /> It would have been okay if the Relics / Advanced Armory and Thaumatechnology were all better / less cost than a Benediction or castigation, but that often was not the case, or rather, it was often enough the reverse.<br /> <br /> I had been hoping with the godmachine update, we might see some different system, say, making the Castigations and Benedictions cost 2 or 3 experience points per dot or rewrite some endowments, but that overall has not been the case...<br /> <br /> I think this often IS a problem because it effectively leads to either no one wanting to play the expensive endowments Conspiracies OR the ones with less cost being banned or of course some self made houserule to rain it in...<br /> <br /> We personally adapted Castigations as 3 experience points per dot and I have to say I found it worked reasonably well.<br /> I was wondering, does anyone else have that problem?<br /> <br /> Or are we the exception, given that it has not been addressed in mortal remains?<br /> <br /> <br /> Two tangential questions:<br /> <br /> 1) How much XP do new Benedictions cost now?<br /> It used to be 5, so, would (after character creation) one dot of Benediction be 1 XP and each new Benediction you can use also 1 experience point (separately)?<br /> <br /> 2) Looking at the Gulf of Hades Castigation, how come that it does not cost Willpower to use?<br /> It is effectively an attack that ignores armor and defense and has a 0L rating with the added benefit of a useful negative condition on the target AND practical applications outside of combat.<br /> The drawback of a dramatic failure is relatively bad, but on the other hand, an exceptional success is VERY rewarding (and since it costs no willpower to use, even quite possible).<br /> I am pretty sure I would see my Story Teller say no to it if I wanted to have this Power and, to be fair, I think I would judge it the same way...<br /> I have not looked at all of the other new Endowments, but, is this not a bit out of line? Especially when compared to some of the extremely enemy specific endowments which are pretty much useless against any opponent not of a certain kind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T08:17:18-07:00","id":125176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/125154-mortal-remains-not-quite-as-much-a-change-to-endwoments-as-i-hoped#post125154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) How much XP do new Benedictions cost now?<br /> It used to be 5, so, would (after character creation) one dot of Benediction be 1 XP and each new Benediction you can use also 1 experience point (separately)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. One Experience. Forgot to note that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T12:17:59-07:00","id":126039,"title":"","content":"They've said this a couple of times, but it's worth noting again: this was not a Chronicle book, a place where there was room for big changes, refocusing fluff, etc. This was a product that had room for a patch-job to get it functional in the new system. That was the scope they were aiming for, and that's what they delivered. You might see a full on GMC-style chronicle book where the writers can tweak, tinker, and tear down what they will, but all this existed to do - besides introduce the monsters beyond the big 3 - was to get it so you could play Vigil characters in a GMC game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T12:21:30-07:00","id":126041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Looking at the Gulf of Hades Castigation, how come that it does not cost Willpower to use?<br /> It is effectively an attack that ignores armor and defense and has a 0L rating with the added benefit of a useful negative condition on the target AND practical applications outside of combat.<br /> The drawback of a dramatic failure is relatively bad, but on the other hand, an exceptional success is VERY rewarding (and since it costs no willpower to use, even quite possible).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not sooooooo OP if you think about it, good for a hunter who want to do something in combat without using &quot;heavy artillery&quot; and mantaining some of combat use , (ok... maybe it need to be resisted for better balance, like substracting resistance from the attack against people), it's worse than using almost any gun or melee weapon better than 0L, and clearly worths than the new version of hellfire (even with the willpower cost, castignation dots-1 of damage is HUGE) or the demonic form of one of the supplements.<br /> <br /> However i do think than much more endowements need update and clarification regarding the GMC rules update...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2896-nemastoncito","name":"Nemastoncito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T02:48:18-07:00","id":126562,"title":"","content":"@Kirby Jerusalem: Granted, though I think rebalancing the Merits (or make castigations and benedictions something a bit different) would have been in the scope...<br /> I mean, really, overall, they are okay with a few exceptions, but Castigations and Benedictions just need a cost raise.<br /> As said, we housruled them to 3 XP per dot and I think that works rather fine.<br /> <br /> About Gulf of Hades:<br /> <br /> It is better than a light melee weapon, no initiative malus and neither defense nor armor, that is more than enough to make up for the lack of bonus damage.<br /> With guns, it depends. It shines against heavily armored opponents or those under cover and it has the advantage of being a perfect hidden weapon which neer needs ammunition.<br /> <br /> ...and, as I said, the possibility of recovering all willpower or three points of damage is sweet...<br /> <br /> The only real drawback it has that it is not effective against non-human targets is one thing, thouugh with mages, changelings, slashers, cultists and likely werecreatures that covers a lot of ground and prometheans also suffer from it if differently.<br /> So, unless you go zombie or mummy hunting, are up against ephemeral creatures or face something similar, it is pretty good.<br /> <br /> Making it resisted, or giving it a willpower cost and reducing the bonus for 5 or more successes (by the way, does the only 3 successes for exceptional success through risking willpower apply here? ^^ ; ) would likely bring it in line though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}